  (text "ICM-42688-P in I2C mode: AP_CS tied high, AP_AD0 low -> address 0x68. Powered from the Nano 3.3 V pin; pull-ups fitted only if the Nano is insufficient." (at 20 22 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 7ca49d27-16f3-4471-ae70-8f922cb1fdfb))
  (text "CHECK BEFORE LAYOUT: RESV pins (2, 3, 7, 10, 11) and INT2/FSYNC (9) are left unconnected here; confirm against the datasheet. Confirm the LGA footprint pad order." (at 20 26 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid c64d95b8-962f-45be-b9f3-42ca7b50071e))
  (text "INT1 goes to a test point only: its 3.3 V level may not read reliably on the 5 V Nano. Poll the FIFO over I2C instead." (at 20 30 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid b0b7d375-f1ec-49cd-8fef-af4b415040e9))
  (text "NANO INTERFACE (replaces the J1201 Qwiic header). 3V3 and GND come from Nano pins 17 and 4 on A1." (at 20 245 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 440243c9-aba0-4466-aef0-fc7cdc0d82ac))
  (text "TP1202 / TP1203 (SCL / SDA): pads with 1.0 mm holes under the two plated holes either side of the Nano Qwiic connector. Solder a short pin or wire through each." (at 20 249 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid a48b9ae3-7776-4592-b409-6873570148f5))
  (text "TP1204-TP1208 (SWDIO, SWCLK, NRST, GND, 3V3): 1.0 mm holes over the Nano SWD test pads, which are on the Nano underside facing this board, under the Qwiic connector." (at 20 253 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 19baa184-73b7-4c5d-a3a3-69e524624f7e))
  (text "Hole positions come from Arduino ABX00142 CAD files, which are older than the Nano in hand: verify against the real board before ordering. Measured: the pad marked 3V3 is 3V3." (at 20 257 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid eb30b19b-8af9-4d09-b117-1d17e36ffa5a))
)
